# Embedded Host Adapter — Telegram WebApp (PS-6)

**Decisions:** DL-13, DL-16  
**Package:** `@app-tour/guest-surface-host` subpath — no portal fork.

---

## 1. Scope

| In scope (PS-6) | Out of scope |
| --------------- | ------------ |
| Detect Telegram WebApp host context | Full Telegram SDK bridge |
| Reuse `resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl` for module deep links | Wallet / payment flows |
| Export types for portal shell chrome suppression | Mini-app auth token exchange |

---

## 2. Detection

```typescript
type EmbeddedMemberPortalHost = "telegram" | null;

/** Returns host kind when running inside Telegram WebApp; null on normal browser. */
function resolveEmbeddedMemberPortalHost(input: {
  readonly userAgent?: string | null;
  readonly searchParams?: URLSearchParams | Readonly<Record<string, string>>;
}): EmbeddedMemberPortalHost;
```

| Signal | Weight |
| ------ | ------ |
| `window.Telegram?.WebApp` (client) | authoritative when present |
| `User-Agent` contains `Telegram` | server hint only |
| `?tgWebApp=1` query (dev smoke) | opt-in override for Playwright |

**Rule:** Server routes MUST NOT trust query override in production — gated by `NODE_ENV !== "production"` or explicit dev host allowlist.

---

## 3. URL builder integration

Embedded hosts use the same module URL builder as marketing egress (PS-3):

```text
resolvePortalMemberModuleUrl({ host, pluginId, moduleId })
  → https://{club}.portal.{root}/me/{module}
```

No absolute shop.* or marketing hardcodes (WRS-001).

---

## 4. Portal shell consequences (future)

| Chrome | Normal browser | Telegram embedded |
| ------ | -------------- | ----------------- |
| Bottom nav | visible | visible (compact safe-area) |
| Marketing cross-links | visible | optional suppress via `data-embedded-host="telegram"` |
| Logout | full session clear | same — DL-17 cache invalidation on logout |

Portal consumption is **wired (PS-6):** `apps/portal/app/me/layout.tsx` sets `data-embedded-host` on `PortalMemberShell` when GSH detects Telegram.

---

